# .trivyignore — Accepted CVE exceptions for trivy image scanning
#
# Format:
#   <CVE-ID>  # <base-image>: <rationale> | Review by: <YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# Policy:
#   - Every entry MUST include: CVE ID, affected image, rationale, and a review date.
#   - Additions require a PR review from at least one other engineer.
#   - Review dates should be set no further than 90 days from acceptance.
#   - Remove entries once an upstream fix is available and the base image is updated.
#
# Example (do not uncomment unless this CVE has been evaluated):
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX  # python:3.14-slim: No fix available upstream; only exploitable
#                   # via direct filesystem access not possible in our runtime config.
#                   # Review by: 2026-06-08

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accepted 2026-08-05 — PENDING SECOND-ENGINEER REVIEW (see Policy above).
#
# Every CVE below reports FixedVersion: none, so no dependency bump or base
# image rebuild clears it. All Python-package CVEs that DID have fixes were
# resolved by upgrading instead (uv.lock), not suppressed here.
#
# Affects: sms-backend and sms-researcher-mcp (both FROM python:3.14-slim,
# Debian trixie). sms-frontend (nginx:alpine) scans clean.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# perl-base 5.40.1-6 — 4 CRITICAL, 4 HIGH. No patched Debian trixie package as
# of 2026-08-05. perl is present only as a base-image dependency; neither
# service invokes perl at runtime, and both run as non-root (UID 10001).
CVE-2026-13221  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, CRITICAL, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-42496  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, CRITICAL, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-57433  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, CRITICAL, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-8376   # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, CRITICAL, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-42497  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-48962  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-57432  # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-9538   # python:3.14-slim: perl-base, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03

# util-linux 2.41-5 family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1,
# libsmartcols1, libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux). Base-image only; the
# services do not shell out to these utilities.
CVE-2026-53615  # python:3.14-slim: util-linux family, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03

# ncurses 6.5+20250216-2 (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin).
# Terminal library, unused by either service at runtime.
CVE-2025-69720  # python:3.14-slim: ncurses family, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03

# Remaining base-image packages with no patched version available.
CVE-2026-41992  # python:3.14-slim: gzip, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03
CVE-2026-54369  # python:3.14-slim: libacl1, HIGH, no upstream fix | Review by: 2026-11-03

# ecdsa 0.19.2 — Minerva timing attack. Upstream has declared this wontfix;
# no released version addresses it. Reaches us transitively via
# python-jose[cryptography]. Migrating off python-jose would remove it.
CVE-2024-23342  # sms-backend: ecdsa via python-jose, HIGH, upstream wontfix | Review by: 2026-11-03
